Feature 1.1: Project Persistence & History
Problem: Currently, all work is lost when a session ends. Sandboxes are ephemeral and there's no save/load functionality. The README promises "ideas into working PoC" but there's no way to revisit or iterate on ideas.

What to Build:

A Project data model that captures: project ID, title, description (the original idea), chat history (messages), generated file manifest, sandbox configuration, creation/update timestamps, and status (draft/in-progress/complete)
A project storage layer — initially using browser IndexedDB (via idb or Dexie) for zero-backend deployment, with an interface/adapter pattern so a server-side database (e.g., Supabase, Vercel KV) can be swapped in later
A "Save Project" action in the chat/header UI that serializes the current session state (from the Zustand store + chat context) into a persistent project record
A "My Projects" dashboard page accessible from the header, showing a card grid of saved projects with title, description excerpt, last modified date, status badge, and quick actions (open, duplicate, delete)
An "Open Project" flow that restores chat history, file tree, and attempts to reconnect to the sandbox (or prompts to recreate it)
Auto-save on meaningful milestones (sandbox created, files generated, command run successfully)
