Technical Architecture Notes for Developers
Storage Strategy
The platform currently has no database. The phased approach should be:

Phase 1-2: Use browser storage (IndexedDB via Dexie.js) + Vercel KV for server-side data. This keeps the "Deploy with Vercel" button working with minimal infra.
Phase 3+: Migrate to a proper database (Supabase recommended — aligns with market trends, provides auth + realtime + storage in one). Abstract all storage behind an adapter interface from Phase 1 to make this migration seamless.
Auth Architecture
The codebase already has arctic@3.7.0 (OAuth library) and jose@6.0.12 (JWT library) installed as dependencies. These should be used for Phase 2 auth rather than adding new libraries. Arctic supports 50+ OAuth providers out-of-the-box.

State Management
The current Zustand + nuqs (URL state) + localStorage pattern works well. New features should follow the same pattern:

Ephemeral UI state → Zustand stores
User preferences → nuqs (URL params) for shareability
Persistent config → localStorage (branding pattern)
Server-side data → SWR with API routes
AI Prompt Architecture
The current single prompt.md file works for Next.js-only generation. For multi-framework support, refactor into:

Code
ai/prompts/
  base.md           — Common rules (loop prevention, error handling)
  nextjs.md         — Next.js-specific instructions
  react-vite.md     — React + Vite instructions
  vue.md            — Vue 3 instructions
  express.md        — Express.js API instructions
  python.md         — Python (Flask/FastAPI) instructions
Compose the final prompt by concatenating base.md + framework-specific file.

Component Architecture
All new components should follow the existing patterns:

shadcn/ui base components in components/ui/
Feature components in components/{feature}/
Server components for data fetching, client components for interactivity
Zod schemas for all data validation
CVA (class-variance-authority) for component variants
Clarifying Questions
Before beginning implementation, the following decisions would benefit from stakeholder input:

Database choice: Should we start with client-side IndexedDB (zero infra, works with the Vercel deploy button) or go straight to Supabase/Vercel Postgres (requires additional setup)?

Auth providers: The plan includes GitHub and Google OAuth. Should we also support Microsoft/Azure AD for enterprise environments? What about email/password?

Multi-tenancy: Should organizations be strictly isolated (separate data stores) or is a shared database with row-level security sufficient?

Deployment targets: The README lists Vercel/AWS/GCP/Azure. Which deploy integration should be built first? Vercel is the most natural fit given the tech stack.

Offline support: Should the platform work offline (PWA with service workers) or is it acceptable to require an internet connection (given AI model calls need connectivity)?

Pricing/quotas: If this will be a commercial product, what usage limits should be enforced? This affects how usage tracking is designed.

Data residency: For enterprise customers, do we need to support data residency requirements (EU, US-only, etc.)? This affects the database and storage architecture.
